<title>USA: CSX Corp Q3 shr rises to $1.04.</title>
<headline>CSX Corp Q3 shr rises to $1.04.</headline>
<dateline>RICHMOND, Va. 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>9/2796		     9/29/95</p>
<p> Shr			  $1.04		    $0.96</p>
<p> Net			222,000		  202,000</p>
<p> Revs		   2,647,000		2,601,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 216,611		  210,485</p>
<p>	   9 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr			  $2.83		    $1.62</p>
<p> Net			602,000		  342,000</p>
<p> Revs		   7,833,000		7,594,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 216,611		  210,485</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers) Full company name is CSX Corp</p>
<p>NOTE: The company said starting with the quarter ended June 28, 1996 it changed its earnings to exclude non-transportation activities from operating revenues and expenses. During the second quarter 1995 the company recorded a $257 million pretax charge to recognize estimated costs of initiatives to revise specific operations.</p>
<p>1995 per share data adjusted to reflect a two-for-one stock split distributed to shareholders in December 1995.</p>
</text>
